    amp_guide_h: "What does my printer need?",
    amp_guide_all_h: "For every printer",
    amp_guide_all_p: "Your phone and printer must be on the same Wi-Fi (no guest network, no mobile data). The IP address is shown on the printer screen under Network, or in your router. If the search finds nothing, type the address and port by hand, for example 192.168.1.42:7125.",
    amp_guide_port: "Port {p}",
    amp_guide_manual: "By hand: {h}",
    gd_bambu_m: "A1, A1 mini, P1P, P1S, P2S, X1, H2D, H2S",
    gd_bambu_s: "Turn on LAN mode on the printer.|Turn on Developer mode there too – without it no app may print.|Type the 8-digit access code from the screen into the app.",
    gd_bambu_n: "In LAN mode, Bambu Handy and the Bambu cloud don't work. Camera on X1, H2 and P2S: also turn on “LAN Only Liveview”.",
    gd_acl_m: "Kobra 3, 3 V2, 3 Max, Kobra 4, S1, S1 Max, Kobra X",
    gd_acl_s: "On the printer screen, turn on LAN mode under Network.|The app then finds the printer by itself, otherwise type IP:18910.",
    gd_acl_n: "In LAN mode, the Anycubic app and cloud don't work. Firmware updates only with LAN mode off. With Rinkhals the Klipper way works too (port 7125). Kobra 2 not yet.",
    gd_klipper_m: "Voron, Sovol, QIDI, Snapmaker U1, rooted Creality, Kobra with Rinkhals, Flashforge with ZMOD",
    gd_klipper_s: "Nothing to turn on: Moonraker is already running if Mainsail or Fluidd work.|If the app asks for an API key: copy it in Mainsail or Fluidd under Settings.",
    gd_klipper_n: "Several printers on one computer (KX-Bridge): ports 7126 to 7135.",
    gd_creality_m: "K1, K1C, K1 Max, K1 SE, K2 family, Hi, Ender-3 V3, K3",
    gd_creality_s: "Connect the printer to Wi-Fi, nothing else to turn on.|If it isn't found: type IP:9999.",
    gd_creality_n: "Enders without Wi-Fi (Ender-3, Ender-3 Pro, V2, S1, V3 SE) only work through OctoPrint on a Raspberry Pi.",
    gd_elegoo_m: "Centauri Carbon (port 3030), Centauri Carbon 2 (port 1883)",
    gd_elegoo_s: "Centauri Carbon: nothing to turn on.|Centauri Carbon 2: turn on “LAN only” on the printer and type the access code from the screen.",
    gd_elegoo_n: "Neptune 1 to 3 have no Wi-Fi → OctoPrint. Neptune 4 → Klipper.",
    gd_flashforge_m: "Adventurer 5M, 5M Pro, AD5X, Creator 5",
    gd_flashforge_s: "On the printer screen, turn on “LAN only” under Network.|Type the check code shown there into the app.",
    gd_flashforge_n: "With “LAN only”, the Flashforge cloud doesn't work. With ZMOD firmware use the Klipper way instead.",
    gd_prusa_m: "MK4, MK3.9, MINI, XL, Core One (PrusaLink)",
    gd_prusa_s: "On the printer screen, turn on PrusaLink under Network.|Type the user “maker” and the password from the screen.",
    gd_prusa_n: "No camera via PrusaLink. The app doesn't show MMU slots yet.",
    gd_octoprint_m: "Any printer on USB to a Raspberry Pi (Ender-3, Neptune 1–3, Prusa MK3 …)",
    gd_octoprint_s: "Tap “Request access” in the app.|Click “Allow” in OctoPrint in your browser – done, no key to type.",
    gd_octoprint_n: "",
